	Following is a random name maker I put together to go with my
citizenmaker. Unlike most stuff on Warhammer II, this should actually work
on most LPmuds, so I thought I'd post it, the names it makes are in pseudo
Japanese, but by simpy maodifying the list of syllables, or making vowells and
consonants instead of just syllables, this can be changed.

		---Akane
(enjoy)

/*
 *		/obj/daemons/namer.c version 1.0
 *	Please retain this header in all versions.
 * This namer made by Akane of Warhammer II .
 *	---Raven Blackburn
 *
 * by changing and adding syllables you should be able to get a drastically
 * different set of names. This version uses Japanese syllables (though some
 * of those it uses are uncommon, all are Japanese). One idea would be to
 * switch the order of vowell and consonant in the syllables, so that
 * it went vowell+consonant=syllable , instead of consonant+vowell=syllable
 * doing such would give drastically different output. Also note that 
 * Japanese has no 'v' or 'l' sounds (they tend to use 'b' or 'r' for
 * these when adopting foriegn words into thier language. (Elf becomes
 * Erufu (looks better written in kana :-) ), since they they write by
 * syllables, but the two 'u's are almost
 * silent. Pronounciation for the vowells in these syllables is:
 * a = ah as in 'hah'	e = eh as in 'pen'
 * i = ee as in 'keep'  o = oh as in 'phone'
 * u = oo as in 'food'
 *
 *	Adopted fro LPmud from a C program I hacked together awhile back.
 *	To use simply do "obj/daemons"->get_name();
 */

